        "plan": "The clinician will arrange a brain MRI to evaluate for secondary causes of headache. The patient was instructed to seek immediate emergency care if the headache becomes sudden and severe, or if she develops fever or neck stiffness, as per safety‑netting advice. Follow‑up will be scheduled after imaging results to discuss findings and further management. No new medications were prescribed at this visit; the patient will continue sertraline as currently taken. Documentation of allergies, surgical history, and social history will be obtained at the next encounter."
